   },
   {
    "primary": {
     "type": "TextChapter",
     "page_section_element_title": [
      {
       "type": "heading6",
       "text": "Using Figma design library",
       "spans": []
      }
     ],
     "page_section_element_body": [
      {
       "type": "paragraph",
       "text": "1. Access the design library: Open your Figma project and locate the design library file (.fig file) that contains the desired design components and styles.",
       "spans": []
      },
      {
       "type": "paragraph",
       "text": "2. Add the design library: Go to the main menu and select \"File\" > \"Add Library to Figma.\" Choose the design library file from your local storage",
       "spans": []
      },
      {
       "type": "paragraph",
       "text": "3. Enable the design library: Once added, enable the design library by selecting \"Plugins\" > \"Manage Libraries\" from the main menu. Enable the library by toggling the switch next to its name.",
       "spans": []
      },
      {
       "type": "paragraph",
       "text": "4. With the design library enabled, you can start using its components in your Figma project. Access the components panel (or use the shortcut \"Cmd+/\") and browse through the library to find the desired components. Drag and drop components onto your canvas.",
       "spans": []
      },
      {
       "type": "paragraph",
       "text": "5. The design library also includes predefined text styles, colour palettes, and other design elements. To apply styles from the library, select the desired text or shape, and choose the appropriate style from the styles panel or the right-click context menu.",
       "spans": []
      }
     ],
     "component_id": null,
